{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 16 right parenthesis squared equals 289\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>289</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the given equation is a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane. The point&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis q comma s right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the circle. Which of the following is NOT a possible value of <math alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["19e976eb-1e2e-45de-b021-e50c38cee8dc"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "19e976eb-1e2e-45de-b021-e50c38cee8dc", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"negative 17\"><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "32ac7351-400b-4727-aa47-009caf9b6164", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"negative 3\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "f89d268c-e2a1-4bdc-971d-2b6ec3e50dc3", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "6f98114c-1b76-4eef-8fe8-b347907d3f2e", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p>Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the graph of the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 16 right parenthesis squared equals 289\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>289</mn></math> is a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane. For a circle in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, its center is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and its radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared equals 289\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>289</mn></math>. Taking the positive square root of both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals 17\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Therefore, the center of this circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 comma negative 16 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math>. It follows that the <em>x</em>-coordinates of the points that lie on the circle must be within <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> units of the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the center of the circle. Therefore, the least possible <em>x</em>-coordinate of a point that lies on the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 minus 17\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 14\"><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></math>, and the greatest possible <em>x</em>-coordinate of a point that lies on the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3 plus 17\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>17</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn></math>. So for any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis q comma s right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></math> to lie on the circle, it must be true that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 14 less than or equals q less than or equals 20\"><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>20</mn></math>. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 17\"><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></math> does not satisfy this inequality, it is NOT a possible value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 3\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> satisfies the inequality&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 14 less than or equals q less than or equals 20\"><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>20</mn></math>, it is a possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn></math> satisfies the inequality&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 14 less than or equals q less than or equals 20\"><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>20</mn></math>, it is a possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> satisfies the inequality&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 14 less than or equals q less than or equals 20\"><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>20</mn></math>, it is a possible value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi></math>.</p>", "externalid": "aa85b05d-ab61-4169-aad8-c85d16b1e1c9", "correct_answer": ["A"]}